														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4456361">
									

<p>Writing seems a bit off in places when the text is supposed to be clinical. Though, I do feel like a jerk for initially taking issue with the &quot;bad&quot; writing of the journal entries before realizing it's styled after indigenous sources of the same nature.</p>
<p>Ultimately, as a retelling of colonialism, the Foundation doesn't do much colonizing. The outbreak is just an unfortunate, holocaustic accident for which the colonizers are only at fault for their negligence. The descriptions of the horrors of the carvers are certainly riveting but I'd like to see more culpability on the part of the Foundation is all?</p>

