					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sebarus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2341265); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2341265&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606380088" alt="Sebarus" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2341265)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sebarus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2341265); return false;" >Sebarus</a></span> <span class="odate time_1577593528 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 Dec 2019 04:25</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4456376">
									

<p>I didn't really have colonialism in mind when writing this, it stemmed more from the thought process of &quot;what if animals never evolved and plants took their place, and what if a voracious, fast-breeding herbivore was then introduced to that ecology&quot;. There is some overlap between the concepts though, since conquistadors brought new diseases to the Americas that devastated much of the indigenous population.</p>
<p>I did think about ways of adding a little piece somewhere that would indicate some sense of guilt on the Foundation's part, but it felt detached.</p>
<p>When it comes to clinical tone errors, if you could point out some of those it would be greatly appreciated. English isn't my first language, so I sometimes struggle to differentiate clinical words from more casual ones.</p>

							</div>

								
					
