<p>Ah, my bad. I suppose that was a bit of an aggressive reading anyways.</p>
<p>Regarding tonal errors (which are fairly subjective and oftentimes only deal-breakers in aggregate):</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Usage of &quot;seem&quot; and &quot;appear&quot; when those words imply that something is not actually true. Definitive language is preferable, because the banana actually does not suffer from normal biological degradation as opposed to merely seeming like it does not.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is indestructible and does not seem to suffer from normal biological degradation. It appears to be ancient, with carbon dating placing it as at least 20,000 years old.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Small thing but consider capitalizing &quot;addendum&quot;?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>See addendum 4823.1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Usage of contractions in an official report.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>On the second day, one of the representatives of the U-3567 Foundation didn't show up to a scheduled meeting.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Injecting irrelevant descriptions into a sentence; the damage sustained by the journal would be better served as its own sentence.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>On 3/6/2020, SCP-4823 unpeeled itself and a journal damaged by moisture was ejected out of it.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Otherwise, other discrepancies from standard wiki writing conventions (<em>e.g.</em> &quot;main anomaly&quot; vs. &quot;primary anomaly&quot;) can be marked up to writer's choice and your unique style. I actually do enjoy your writing style here, for what it's worth; it's in line with the conventions of clinical tone but still very distinctive.</p>

							</div>

								
					
