<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I want to say that you have my respect Sebarus since in my reading I couldn’t tell that English was not your 1st language and I admire anyone that can speak multiple languages especially english since it is one if not the most complicated language still spoken and on top of that your article is definitely one of my favorite writing pieces since it got me thinking about cross-contamination of ecosystems and made me decide that if we encounter new lifeforms then it wouldn’t be like Star Trek where everyone goes down to the surface to meat the locals. Instead the way we would have to communicate is to be separated by layers of thick metal and glass or have inches of hazmat suit to protect the alien world from cross-contamination as even things like benign intestinal bacteria could be the deadliest biohazard when the whole evolutionary history of the planet didn’t have to deal with it and if your intent IS to colonize and you want to invade the planet remember that their diseases can work just as well as yours so you would have to fight in clunky hazmat suits while fighting an entire planet of beings while some of them may be sentient being with advanced civilization with an organized military that may have used unique resources on their planet to build weapons that you have no knowledge about so developing counter-measures would take years to make meanwhile your troops would be defenseless against it and on top of that you would have to deal with local wildlife that you have again no knowledge of until you have to deal with them while the locals would already have ways to deal with said wildlife (Something on our world would be bears we have items like bear mace and know to keep anything that has food in it or has had food in it up high out of the bears reach, while aliens would have to invent their own counter-measures after they get all their food eaten and have a lost a few people that got to close too a mother’s cub or made a sudden or aggressive movement)</p>
<p>Ok to wrap this up after getting off topic an invasion of another world that is already inhabited would be almost impossible and the only scenario I can think of that would end in a victory for the invaders is if the defending world has inferior military technology, lacks the ability to travel to the invader’s planet, the invaders can gather huge amounts of intelligence on everything the defenders do from building bombs to dealing with wildlife, and the invaders can transport soldiers and supplies in a efficient and cost-effective manner as they would need vast amounts of both, and to top all that they would need to create a airtight suit that can be effective in a combat situation (research into mechs would be recommended). I can make this list go on longer but I would need to write an essay to do the topic justice.</p>
