			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4777541">
									

<p>Well the thing is Baseline wasn’t trying to colonize U-3567 the fruit flys where an accident but if they were to use SCP-2000 there would be a few problems</p>
<p>1. In order to cross dimensions you are required to peel the banana how would you get SCP-2000 a <span style="text-decoration: underline;">large machine</span> along with the huge severs the Foundation stores the data of everyone on the planet to peel the banana as they can’t have all that being carried by one person.</p>
<p>2. SCP-2000 leaves humans with all the memories they have since their profile was last updated so how would the recently spawned humans react to waking up on a planet that is completely deferent then the one they were on “yesterday”</p>
<p>3. Using SCP-2000 would create a double of almost every human imagine the confusion that would create when dealing with the population assuming that you are importing goods from the U-3567 colonies</p>
<p>4. With all the humans suddenly spawning in on the alien world it is safe to assume that the panic would plunge the world into anarchy as they struggled to survive among the ruined wastes as the food from the banana corpses run out since without the bananas the local livestock would starve getting rid of the only possible food source and I believe that this chaos would make building a colony harder not easier</p>
<p>5. And finally the O5s would never approve moving something as vital to the Foundation as<br />
SCP-2000 to another universe as it could be lost or damaged along the way there by dooming the baseline since that fact that they need SCP-2000 proves that without it they are doomed.</p>

							</div>

